# RFC 9755 does not require this, but a mailbox whose UTF-8 name could
# also be read as mUTF-7 is ambiguous: a connection that has not enabled
# UTF8=ACCEPT can only report it by escaping the ampersand. We would
# rather not have such names at all, so creating one is refused. A name
# that cannot be mUTF-7 is of course still fine.
depends twologins
use second
send 1
a enable utf8=accept
receive 2
* ENABLED UTF8=ACCEPT
a OK done
send 1
b create &CQkJJgk+CTkJMAkj-
receive 1
b NO Mailbox name could also be read as mUTF-7
send 2
c create {18+}
उदाहरण
receive 1
c OK done
end
